# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. Never commit .env.
# Faz 1 (backtest only) bu key'leri GEREKTIRMEZ — data.binance.vision public.
# Bu dosya Faz 2+ (paper / live) için referans.

# --- Binance API (REQUIRED for `live-trade` command, not for paper) ---
#
# CRITICAL SECURITY SETUP — follow exactly:
#   1. Sign in to https://www.binance.com → Profile icon → "API Management"
#   2. Click "Create API" → "System Generated"
#   3. Name it (e.g. "quant-trader-mainnet"), complete 2FA verification
#   4. ⚠️ EDIT RESTRICTIONS ⚠️:
#         ✓ Enable Spot & Margin Trading
#         ✗ Enable Futures             ← LEAVE UNCHECKED
#         ✗ Enable Withdrawals         ← LEAVE UNCHECKED (HARD REQUIREMENT)
#         ✓ Restrict access to trusted IPs only
#             → Add this machine's public IP. Find it via:
#               curl ifconfig.me
#   5. Save. Copy API Key + Secret Key into the lines below.
#      (Secret is shown ONCE — keep it safe. Lose it → recreate the key.)
#
# The system performs a pre-flight check on every `live-trade` run and
# REFUSES TO START if "Enable Withdrawals" is on. This is your safety net.
#
# For TESTNET (recommended first run, fake money):
#   • Get keys at https://testnet.binance.vision
#   • Use the same env vars; system uses testnet endpoint when --testnet flag set
BINANCE_API_KEY=
BINANCE_API_SECRET=

# --- Telegram (paper trader live mode alerts) ---
# OPTIONAL. If both vars set, `paper-trade --live` sends notifications to
# your Telegram chat. Otherwise live mode runs console-only.
#
# Setup (one-time, ~2 minutes):
#   1. In Telegram, message @BotFather → /newbot → name it, get TOKEN.
#   2. Open your new bot in Telegram, hit "Start" so it has permission
#      to message you.
#   3. Send the bot any test message.
#   4. curl "https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates"
#      → find result[0].message.chat.id (integer, may be negative).
#   5. Fill below and copy this file to .env (.env is gitignored).
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
